  "Number": 30,
  "Question": "A house worth \\(\\$9000\\) is sold by Mr. \\(A\\) to Mr. \\(B\\) at a \\(10\\%\\) loss. Mr. \\(B\\) sells the house back to Mr. \\(A\\) at a \\(10\\%\\) gain. The result of the two transactions is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Mr. \\(A\\) breaks even",
    "B": "Mr. \\(B\\) gains \\(\\$900\\)",
    "C": "Mr. \\(A\\) loses \\(\\$900\\)",
    "D": "Mr. \\(A\\) loses \\(\\$810\\)",
    "E": "Mr. \\(B\\) gains \\(\\$1710\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The two percentages use different price bases. Mr. A's \\(10\\%\\) loss is based on \\(\\$9000\\), so the first sale price is\n\\[\n9000-0.10(9000)=8100.\n\\]\nMr. B's \\(10\\%\\) gain is based on the \\(\\$8100\\) he paid. He therefore sells the house back for\n\\[\n8100+0.10(8100)=8910.\n\\]\nMr. A finishes with the same house he started with, but he has paid \\(8910-8100=810\\) dollars more than he received. Thus Mr. A loses \\(\\$810\\), choice D.",
